  "Question": "A makes \\(x\\) items per day, and B makes 2 more items per day than A. A takes the same amount of time to make 60 items as B takes to make 80 items. Find \\(x\\).",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "6",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Set up the equation \\(\\frac{60}{x}=\\frac{80}{x+2}\\). Clearing the denominators gives \\(60(x+2)=80x\\), so \\(x=6\\). Checking confirms that it satisfies the conditions of the problem.\n\nAlternative method 1: Find the common duration\n\nOver the same duration, B makes \\(80-60=20\\) more items because B makes 2 more items each day. Thus the common duration is \\(20\\div2=10\\) days. A therefore makes \\(x=60\\div10=6\\) items per day. B makes 8 items per day, consistent with making 80 items in those 10 days.",
